WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.297
Easy Folk Tales. The Fisherman and His Wife.

00:00:03.297 --> 00:00:07.951
A poor fisherman lived with his wife in a small, dirty house by the sea.

00:00:07.951 --> 00:00:10.138
One day he caught a large fish.

00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:12.377
"Please let me go," said the fish.

00:00:12.377 --> 00:00:14.078
"I am not a real fish.

00:00:14.078 --> 00:00:15.252
I am a prince."

00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:19.700
The fisherman was a kind man, and he put the fish back in the water.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.349
When he told his wife, she was angry.

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:25.100
"A magic fish, and you asked for nothing?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.716
Go back and ask for a nice little house."

00:00:27.716 --> 00:00:30.760
The fisherman went back to the sea and called the fish.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.400
"My wife wants a little house," he said.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.350
"Go home," said the fish.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.697
"She has it already."

00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:40.573
And there she was, standing at the door of a pretty house.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.261
But after a week she said, "This house is too small.

00:00:44.261 --> 00:00:46.692
I want to live in a great stone castle."

00:00:46.692 --> 00:00:49.588
The fisherman did not want to go, but he went.

00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:51.451
The sea was dark and gray.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.401
"Go home," said the fish.

00:00:53.401 --> 00:00:55.599
"She is standing at the castle door."

00:00:55.599 --> 00:00:59.283
The next morning his wife said, "I want to be king."

00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:01.063
And the fish made her king.

00:01:01.063 --> 00:01:05.774
Then she wanted to be queen of the whole world, and the fish gave her that too.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:08.753
The sea was black now, and the wind was strong.

00:01:08.753 --> 00:01:10.783
But still she was not happy.

00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:13.261
One morning she watched the sun come up.

00:01:13.261 --> 00:01:16.016
"Husband," she said, "go to the fish.

00:01:16.016 --> 00:01:18.428
I want to make the sun and the moon come up.

00:01:18.428 --> 00:01:20.081
I want to be like God."

00:01:20.081 --> 00:01:22.213
The fisherman went down to the sea.

00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:24.072
There was a terrible storm.

00:01:24.072 --> 00:01:25.739
He shouted to the fish.

00:01:25.739 --> 00:01:27.689
"Go home," said the fish.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:30.270
"She is sitting in your little old house again."

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.296
And there they are living to this day.
